The lecture’s own before-and-after contrast can then be written as $P_{\mathrm{comm},\mathrm{now}} > P_{\mathrm{comm},\mathrm{past}}.$ Once that condition is in place, remote work becomes more feasible: $\begin{aligned}
V_{\mathrm{remote}} &= h(P_{\mathrm{comm}}),\\
\frac{dh}{dP_{\mathrm{comm}}} &> 0.\end{aligned}$ Putting the two layers together gives the compact chain $B\uparrow,\ C\uparrow
\;\Longrightarrow\;
P_{\mathrm{comm}}\uparrow
\;\Longrightarrow\;
V_{\mathrm{remote}}\uparrow.$

